{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.graded_two_anchor_nogo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.graded_two_anchor_nogo","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L100-L117","doc":"**(N) the two-anchor NO-GO.** For every `q ≥ 1`, if the graded dimension reaches\nthe A=3 strong target (`[3]_q ≥ ρ_strong(3) = 3.8128`), then it strictly overshoots\nthe A=4 strong target: `ρ_grad(4) = [3]_q·[4]_q > ρ_strong(4) = 13.0316`, because\n`[4]_q ≥ 4` (step-lock) and `3.8128 · 4 = 15.2512 > 13.0316`.\n\nHence **no single parameter-free `q` lands both light-nucleus anchors**: the\none-parameter `q`-scaled coinvariant graded dimension `[A]_q!` cannot close the\nΔ_λ magnitude wall. The `2.2196` MeV-ratio no-go margin certifies that closing the\nbracket requires a genuinely `A`-dependent (non-single-knob) damping — the `q`-knob\nalone cannot tighten the two-sided bracket to the observed magnitudes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio4_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio4_mono","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L80-L98","doc":"**(M) single-knob monotonicity, A=4.** `q ↦ ρ_grad(4) = [3]_q·[4]_q` is monotone\non `[1,∞)`. Together with `gradedRatio3_mono`, the single knob `q` moves BOTH the\nA=3 and A=4 ratios upward — it cannot push one up and the other down. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L76-L78","doc":"Positivity of `[4]_q` on `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Positivity of `[3]_q` on `q ≥ 1` (used for the product monotonicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3_mono","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**(M) single-knob monotonicity, A=3.** `q ↦ [3]_q` is monotone on `[1,∞)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_gt_data_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_gt_data_step","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L56-L63","doc":"**(S′) graded step strictly exceeds the data step for every `q ≥ 1`.**\nThe isospin-corrected data step `ρ_strong(4)/ρ_strong(3) = 13.0316/3.8128 ≈ 3.418`\nis `< 4 ≤ [4]_q`, so no `q ≥ 1` flattens the graded step to the observed growth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_ge_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4_ge_four","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L48-L54","doc":"**(S) step-lock.** For `q ≥ 1`, the graded A=3→A=4 step `[4]_q ≥ 4`.\nExact factorisation `[4]_q − 4 = (q−1)(q² + 2q + 3)`, non-negative on `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedStep4","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L44-L46","doc":"`[4]_q = 1 + q + q² + q³`, the multiplicative A=3→A=4 graded step\n(`ρ_grad(4) = gradedRatio3 · gradedStep4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.gradedRatio3","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationTwoAnchorNoGo.lean#L41-L42","doc":"`ρ_grad(3) = W_3/W_2 = [3]_q = 1 + q + q²` (the A=3 coinvariant graded ratio). ","signatureChunk":0}]}